80bba405-3691-40ad-9732-c275d824d161	00e56846-b7b1-43ce-96a7-7ddce76d2461	44bfea88-03c6-4311-85f4-30dcd2b5a78d	VAPT Report — google project 5	**Executive Summary: Security Posture of Test Security V2**\n\nThe recent Vulnerability Assessment and Penetration Testing (VAPT) report for the Google Project 5 has identified key security concerns that require immediate attention. The security posture of Test Security V2 is currently vulnerable to potential attacks, with findings indicating a lack of input validation and insecure interface configurations.\n\nSystemic themes observed in the findings include weaknesses in user input handling and inadequate security controls in the administrative interface. The presence of an HTML Injection vulnerability in the Admin Interface is particularly concerning, as it could allow an attacker to inject malicious code and potentially compromise the application.\n\nThe business risk associated with these findings is significant, posing a threat to data integrity and regulatory compliance. If exploited, these vulnerabilities could lead to data exfiltration, reputational damage, and financial losses.\n\nTo mitigate these risks, we recommend the following strategic actions:\n* Implement robust input validation and sanitization mechanisms to prevent malicious code injection\n* Conduct a comprehensive review of administrative interface configurations to ensure alignment with security best practices\n* Develop and enforce a regular security testing and vulnerability management program to identify and address potential weaknesses proactively	\N	\N	final	standard_vapt	c416a71f-bc6b-4ee0-898b-f5fd4b32b98f	1	\N	\N	https://ypgtxilmkiwitsiythpm.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/poc-files/44bfea88-03c6-4311-85f4-30dcd2b5a78d/reports/vapt-report-44bfea88-03c6-4311-85f4-30dcd2b5a78d-2026-05-17T20-57-04-016Z.docx	\N	idle	2026-05-17 20:57:04.068375+00	2026-05-17 20:57:04.310014+00	\N
