uest(ZapApiHandler.java:111)\n\tat org.zaproxy.addon.network.internal.server.http.handlers.ZapApiHandler.handleRequest(ZapApiHandler.java:85)\n\tat org.zaproxy.addon.network.internal.server.http.handlers.ZapApiHandler.handleMessage(ZapApiHandler.java:70)\n\tat org.zaproxy.addon.network.internal.server.http.MainServerHandler.notifyMessageHandlers(MainServerHandler.java:151)\n\tat org.zaproxy.addon.network.internal.server.http.MainServerHandler.processMessage(MainServerHandler.java:131)\n\tat org.zaproxy.addon.network.internal.server.http.LocalServerHandler.processMessage(LocalServerHandler.java:67)\n\tat org.zaproxy.addon.network.i	{"site": [{"@ssl": "true", "@host": "zero.webappsecurity.com", "@name": "https://zero.webappsecurity.com", "@port": "443", "alerts": []}, {"@ssl": "false", "@host": "zero.webappsecurity.com", "@name": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com", "@port": "80", "alerts": [{"desc": "<p>Content Security Policy (CSP) is an added layer of security that helps to detect and mitigate certain types of attacks, including Cross Site Scripting (XSS) and data injection attacks. These attacks are used for everything from data theft to site defacement or distribution of malware. CSP provides a set of standard HTTP headers that allow website owners to declare approved sources of content that browsers should be allowed to load on that page — covered types are JavaScript, CSS, HTML frames, fonts, images and embeddable objects such as Java applets, ActiveX, audio and video files.</p>", "name": "Content Security Policy (CSP) Header Not Set", "alert": "Content Security Policy (CSP) Header Not Set", "count": "5", "cweid": "693", "wascid": "15", "alertRef": "10038-1", "pluginid": "10038", "riskcode": "2", "riskdesc": "Medium (High)", "solution": "<p>Ensure that your web server, application server, load balancer, etc. is configured to set the Content-Security-Policy header.</p>", "sourceid": "1", "systemic": true, "instances": [{"id": "1", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/", "otherinfo": ""}, {"id": "36", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/dashboard", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/dashboard", "otherinfo": ""}, {"id": "17", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/help.html", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/help.html", "otherinfo": ""}, {"id": "23", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/index.html", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/index.html", "otherinfo": ""}, {"id": "7", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/search.html", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/search.html", "otherinfo": ""}], "otherinfo": "", "reference": "<p>https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/CSP</p><p>https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Content_Security_Policy_Cheat_Sheet.html</p><p>https://www.w3.org/TR/CSP/</p><p>https://w3c.github.io/webappsec-csp/</p><p>https://web.dev/articles/csp</p><p>https://caniuse.com/#feat=contentsecuritypolicy</p><p>https://content-security-policy.com/</p>", "confidence": "3"}, {"desc": "<p>Web browser data loading may be possible, due to a Cross Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) misconfiguration on the web server.</p>", "name": "Cross-Domain Misconfiguration", "alert": "Cross-Domain Misconfiguration", "count": "5", "cweid": "264", "wascid": "14", "alertRef": "10098", "pluginid": "10098", "riskcode": "2", "riskdesc": "Medium (Medium)", "solution": "<p>Ensure that sensitive data is not available in an unauthenticated manner (using IP address white-listing, for instance).</p><p>Configure the \\"Access-Control-Allow-Origin\\" HTTP header to a more restrictive set of domains, or remove all CORS headers entirely, to allow the web browser to enforce the Same Origin Policy (SOP) in a more restrictive manner.</p>", "sourceid": "1", "systemic": true, "instances": [{"id": "2", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/", "otherinfo": "The CORS misconfiguration on the web server permits cross-domain read requests from arbitrary third party domains, using unauthenticated APIs on this domain. Web browser implementations do not permit arbitrary third parties to read the response from authenticated APIs, however. This reduces the risk somewhat. This misconfiguration could be used by an attacker to access data that is available in an unauthenticated manner, but which uses some other form of security, such as IP address white-listing."}, {"id": "6", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/logout.html", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/logout.html", "otherinfo": "The CORS misconfiguration on the web server permits cross-domain read requests from arbitrary third party domains, using unauthenticated APIs on this domain. Web browser implementations do not permit arbitrary third parties to read the response from authenticated APIs, however. This reduces the risk somewhat. This misconfiguration could be used by an attacker to access data that is available in an unauthenticated manner, but which uses some other form of security, such as IP address white-listing."}, {"id": "14", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/resources/js/bootstrap.min.js", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/resources/js/bootstrap.min.js", "otherinfo": "The CORS misconfiguration on the web server permits cross-domain read requests from arbitrary third party domains, using unauthenticated APIs on this domain. Web browser implementations do not permit arbitrary third parties to read the response from authenticated APIs, however. This reduces the risk somewhat. This misconfiguration could be used by an attacker to access data that is available in an unauthenticated manner, but which uses some other form of security, such as IP address white-listing."}, {"id": "8", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/resources/js/placeholders.min.js", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/resources/js/placeholders.min.js", "otherinfo": "The CORS misconfiguration on the web server permits cross-domain read requests from arbitrary third party domains, using unauthenticated APIs on this domain. Web browser implementations do not permit arbitrary third parties to read the response from authenticated APIs, however. This reduces the risk somewhat. This misconfiguration could be used by an attacker to access data that is available in an unauthenticated manner, but which uses some other form of security, such as IP address white-listing."}, {"id": "11", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/search.html", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/search.html", "otherinfo": "The CORS misconfiguration on the web server permits cross-domain read requests from arbitrary third party domains, using unauthenticated APIs on this domain. Web browser implementations do not permit arbitrary third parties to read the response from authenticated APIs, however. This reduces the risk somewhat. This misconfiguration could be used by an attacker to access data that is available in an unauthenticated manner, but which uses some other form of security, such as IP address white-listing."}], "otherinfo": "<p>The CORS misconfiguration on the web server permits cross-domain read requests from arbitrary third party domains, using unauthenticated APIs on this domain. Web browser implementations do not permit arbitrary third parties to read the response from authenticated APIs, however. This reduces the risk somewhat. This misconfiguration could be used by an attacker to access data that is available in an unauthenticated manner, but which uses some other form of security, such as IP address white-listing.</p>", "reference": "<p>https://vulncat.fortify.com/en/detail?category=HTML5&subcategory=Overly%20Permissive%20CORS%20Policy</p>", "confidence": "2"}, {"desc": "<p>The site is only served under HTTP and not HTTPS.</p>", "name": "HTTP Only Site", "alert": "HTTP Only Site", "count": "1", "cweid": "311", "wascid": "4", "alertRef": "10106", "pluginid": "10106", "riskcode": "2", "riskdesc": "Medium (Medium)", "solution": "<p>Configure your web or application server to use SSL (https).</p>", "sourceid": "498", "systemic": false, "instances": [{"id": "1464", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "", "nodeName": "https://zero.webappsecurity.com/", "otherinfo": "Failed to connect.\\nZAP attempted to connect via: https://zero.webappsecurity.com/"}], "otherinfo": "<p>Failed to connect.</p><p>ZAP attempted to connect via: https://zero.webappsecurity.com/</p>", "reference": "<p>https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Transport_Layer_Protection_Cheat_Sheet.html</p><p>https://letsencrypt.org/</p>", "confidence": "2"}, {"desc": "<p>A sensitive file was identified as accessible or available. This may leak administrative, configuration, or credential information which can be leveraged by a malicious individual to further attack the system or conduct social engineering efforts.</p>", "name": "Hidden File Found", "alert": "Hidden File Found", "count": "1", "cweid": "538", "wascid": "13", "alertRef": "40035", "pluginid": "40035", "riskcode": "2", "riskdesc": "Medium (High)", "solution": "<p>Consider whether or not the component is actually required in production, if it isn't then disable it. If it is then ensure access to it requires appropriate authentication and authorization, or limit exposure to internal systems or specific source IPs, etc.</p>", "sourceid": "517", "systemic": false, "instances": [{"id": "1465", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/server-status", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "HTTP/1.1 200 OK", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/server-status", "otherinfo": "apache_server_status"}], "otherinfo": "<p>apache_server_status</p>", "reference": "<p>https://blog.hboeck.de/archives/892-Introducing-Snallygaster-a-Tool-to-Scan-for-Secrets-on-Web-Servers.html</p><p>https://httpd.apache.org/docs/current/mod/mod_status.html</p>", "confidence": "3"}, {"desc": "<p>The response does not protect against 'ClickJacking' attacks. It should include either Content-Security-Policy with 'frame-ancestors' directive or X-Frame-Options.</p>", "name": "Missing Anti-clickjacking Header", "alert": "Missing Anti-clickjacking Header", "count": "4", "cweid": "1021", "wascid": "15", "alertRef": "10020-1", "pluginid": "10020", "riskcode": "2", "riskdesc": "Medium (Medium)", "solution": "<p>Modern Web browsers support the Content-Security-Policy and X-Frame-Options HTTP headers. Ensure one of them is set on all web pages returned by your site/app.</p><p>If you expect the page to be framed only by pages on your server (e.g. it's part of a FRAMESET) then you'll want to use SAMEORIGIN, otherwise if you never expect the page to be framed, you should use DENY. Alternatively consider implementing Content Security Policy's \\"frame-ancestors\\" directive.</p>", "sourceid": "1", "systemic": false, "instances": [{"id": "0", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/", "param": "x-frame-options", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/", "otherinfo": ""}, {"id": "10", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/help.html", "param": "x-frame-options", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/help.html", "otherinfo": ""}, {"id": "12", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/index.html", "param": "x-frame-options", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/index.html", "otherinfo": ""}, {"id": "211", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/search.html?searchTerm=ZAP", "param": "x-frame-options", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/search.html (searchTerm)", "otherinfo": ""}], "otherinfo": "", "reference": "<p>https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/X-Frame-Options</p>", "confidence": "2"}, {"desc": "<p>The identified library appears to be vulnerable.</p>", "name": "Vulnerable JS Library", "alert": "Vulnerable JS Library", "count": "1", "cweid": "1395", "wascid": "-1", "alertRef": "10003", "pluginid": "10003", "riskcode": "2", "riskdesc": "Medium (Medium)", "solution": "<p>Upgrade to the latest version of the affected library.</p>", "sourceid": "13", "systemic": false, "instances": [{"id": "67", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/resources/js/jquery-1.8.2.min.js", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "jquery-1.8.2.min.js", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/resources/js/jquery-1.8.2.min.js", "otherinfo": "The identified library jquery, version 1.8.2 is vulnerable.\\nCVE-2020-11023\\nCVE-2015-9251\\nCVE-2019-11358\\nCVE-2020-7656\\nCVE-2012-6708\\nhttps://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2012-6708\\nhttps://github.com/jquery/jquery/issues/2432\\nhttp://research.insecurelabs.org/jquery/test/\\nhttps://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2019-11358\\nhttps://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rmxg-73gg-4p98\\nhttps://bugs.jquery.com/ticket/11974\\nhttps://github.com/jquery/jquery.com/issues/162\\nhttps://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2020-7656\\nhttp://blog.jquery.com/2016/01/08/jquery-2-2-and-1-12-released/\\nhttp://bugs.jqu