 "Low (High)", "solution": "<p>Configure the server to prevent such information leaks. For example:</p><p>Under Tomcat this is done via the \\"server\\" directive and implementation of custom error pages.</p><p>Under Apache this is done via the \\"ServerSignature\\" and \\"ServerTokens\\" directives.</p>", "sourceid": "31", "systemic": true, "instances": [{"id": "82", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/about", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Tomcat/7.0.70", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/about", "otherinfo": "There is a chance that the highlight in the finding is on a value in the headers, versus the actual matched string in the response body."}, {"id": "38", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/dashboard", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Tomcat/7.0.70", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/dashboard", "otherinfo": "There is a chance that the highlight in the finding is on a value in the headers, versus the actual matched string in the response body."}, {"id": "44", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/home", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Tomcat/7.0.70", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/home", "otherinfo": "There is a chance that the highlight in the finding is on a value in the headers, versus the actual matched string in the response body."}, {"id": "71", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/login", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Tomcat/7.0.70", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/login", "otherinfo": "There is a chance that the highlight in the finding is on a value in the headers, versus the actual matched string in the response body."}, {"id": "18", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/search.html", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Tomcat/7.0.70", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/search.html", "otherinfo": "There is a chance that the highlight in the finding is on a value in the headers, versus the actual matched string in the response body."}], "otherinfo": "<p>There is a chance that the highlight in the finding is on a value in the headers, versus the actual matched string in the response body.</p>", "reference": "<p>https://owasp.org/www-project-web-security-testing-guide/v41/4-Web_Application_Security_Testing/08-Testing_for_Error_Handling/</p>", "confidence": "3"}, {"desc": "<p>The web/application server is leaking version information via the \\"Server\\" HTTP response header. Access to such information may facilitate attackers identifying other vulnerabilities your web/application server is subject to.</p>", "name": "Server Leaks Version Information via \\"Server\\" HTTP Response Header Field", "alert": "Server Leaks Version Information via \\"Server\\" HTTP Response Header Field", "count": "5", "cweid": "497", "wascid": "13", "alertRef": "10036-2", "pluginid": "10036", "riskcode": "1", "riskdesc": "Low (High)", "solution": "<p>Ensure that your web server, application server, load balancer, etc. is configured to suppress the \\"Server\\" header or provide generic details.</p>", "sourceid": "1", "systemic": true, "instances": [{"id": "4", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Apache-Coyote/1.1", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/", "otherinfo": ""}, {"id": "25", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/help.html", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Apache-Coyote/1.1", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/help.html", "otherinfo": ""}, {"id": "9", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/logout.html", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Apache-Coyote/1.1", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/logout.html", "otherinfo": ""}, {"id": "15", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/resources/js/placeholders.min.js", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Apache-Coyote/1.1", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/resources/js/placeholders.min.js", "otherinfo": ""}, {"id": "20", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/search.html", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Apache-Coyote/1.1", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/search.html", "otherinfo": ""}], "otherinfo": "", "reference": "<p>https://httpd.apache.org/docs/current/mod/core.html#servertokens</p><p>https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/msp-n-p/ff648552(v=pandp.10)</p><p>https://www.troyhunt.com/shhh-dont-let-your-response-headers/</p>", "confidence": "3"}, {"desc": "<p>The Anti-MIME-Sniffing header X-Content-Type-Options was not set to 'nosniff'. This allows older versions of Internet Explorer and Chrome to perform MIME-sniffing on the response body, potentially causing the response body to be interpreted and displayed as a content type other than the declared content type. Current (early 2014) and legacy versions of Firefox will use the declared content type (if one is set), rather than performing MIME-sniffing.</p>", "name": "X-Content-Type-Options Header Missing", "alert": "X-Content-Type-Options Header Missing", "count": "5", "cweid": "693", "wascid": "15", "alertRef": "10021", "pluginid": "10021", "riskcode": "1", "riskdesc": "Low (Medium)", "solution": "<p>Ensure that the application/web server sets the Content-Type header appropriately, and that it sets the X-Content-Type-Options header to 'nosniff' for all web pages.</p><p>If possible, ensure that the end user uses a standards-compliant and modern web browser that does not perform MIME-sniffing at all, or that can be directed by the web application/web server to not perform MIME-sniffing.</p>", "sourceid": "1", "systemic": true, "instances": [{"id": "5", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/", "param": "x-content-type-options", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/", "otherinfo": "This issue still applies to error type pages (401, 403, 500, etc.) 