ution": "<p>Configure the server to prevent such information leaks. For example:</p><p>Under Tomcat this is done via the \\"server\\" directive and implementation of custom error pages.</p><p>Under Apache this is done via the \\"ServerSignature\\" and \\"ServerTokens\\" directives.</p>", "sourceid": "23", "systemic": true, "instances": [{"id": "51", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/dashboard", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Tomcat/7.0.70", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/dashboard", "otherinfo": "There is a chance that the highlight in the finding is on a value in the headers, versus the actual matched string in the response body."}, {"id": "49", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/home", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Tomcat/7.0.70", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/home", "otherinfo": "There is a chance that the highlight in the finding is on a value in the headers, versus the actual matched string in the response body."}, {"id": "58", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/login", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Tomcat/7.0.70", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/login", "otherinfo": "There is a chance that the highlight in the finding is on a value in the headers, versus the actual matched string in the response body."}, {"id": "10", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/search.html", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Tomcat/7.0.70", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/search.html", "otherinfo": "There is a chance that the highlight in the finding is on a value in the headers, versus the actual matched string in the response body."}, {"id": "67", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/signup", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Tomcat/7.0.70", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/signup", "otherinfo": "There is a chance that the highlight in the finding is on a value in the headers, versus the actual matched string in the response body."}], "otherinfo": "<p>There is a chance that the highlight in the finding is on a value in the headers, versus the actual matched string in the response body.</p>", "reference": "<p>https://owasp.org/www-project-web-security-testing-guide/v41/4-Web_Application_Security_Testing/08-Testing_for_Error_Handling/</p>", "confidence": "3"}, {"desc": "<p>The web/application server is leaking version information via the \\"Server\\" HTTP response header. Access to such information may facilitate attackers identifying other vulnerabilities your web/application server is subject to.</p>", "name": "Server Leaks Version Information via \\"Server\\" HTTP Response Header Field", "alert": "Server Leaks Version Information via \\"Server\\" HTTP Response Header Field", "count": "5", "cweid": "497", "wascid": "13", "alertRef": "10036-2", "pluginid": "10036", "riskcode": "1", "riskdesc": "Low (High)", "solution": "<p>Ensure that your web server, application server, load balancer, etc. is configured to suppress the \\"Server\\" header or provide generic details.</p>", "sourceid": "1", "systemic": true, "instances": [{"id": "4", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Apache-Coyote/1.1", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/", "otherinfo": ""}, {"id": "9", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/logout.html", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Apache-Coyote/1.1", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/logout.html", "otherinfo": ""}, {"id": "19", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/resources/css/main.css", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Apache-Coyote/1.1", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/resources/css/main.css", "otherinfo": ""}, {"id": "21", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/resources/img/main_carousel_1.jpg", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Apache-Coyote/1.1", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/resources/img/main_carousel_1.jpg", "otherinfo": ""}, {"id": "11", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/search.html", "param": "", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "Apache-Coyote/1.1", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/search.html", "otherinfo": ""}], "otherinfo": "", "reference": "<p>https://httpd.apache.org/docs/current/mod/core.html#servertokens</p><p>https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/previous-versions/msp-n-p/ff648552(v=pandp.10)</p><p>https://www.troyhunt.com/shhh-dont-let-your-response-headers/</p>", "confidence": "3"}, {"desc": "<p>The Anti-MIME-Sniffing header X-Content-Type-Options was not set to 'nosniff'. This allows older versions of Internet Explorer and Chrome to perform MIME-sniffing on the response body, potentially causing the response body to be interpreted and displayed as a content type other than the declared content type. Current (early 2014) and legacy versions of Firefox will use the declared content type (if one is set), rather than performing MIME-sniffing.</p>", "name": "X-Content-Type-Options Header Missing", "alert": "X-Content-Type-Options Header Missing", "count": "5", "cweid": "693", "wascid": "15", "alertRef": "10021", "pluginid": "10021", "riskcode": "1", "riskdesc": "Low (Medium)", "solution": "<p>Ensure that the application/web server sets the Content-Type header appropriately, and that it sets the X-Content-Type-Options header to 'nosniff' for all web pages.</p><p>If possible, ensure that the end user uses a standards-compliant and modern web browser that does not perform MIME-sniffing at all, or that can be directed by the web application/web server to not perform MIME-sniffing.</p>", "sourceid": "1", "systemic": true, "instances": [{"id": "5", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/", "param": "x-content-type-options", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/", "otherinfo": "This issue still applies to error type pages (401, 403, 500, etc.) as those pages are often still affected by injection issues, in which case there is still concern for browsers sniffing pages away from their actual content type.\\nAt \\"High\\" threshold this scan rule will not alert on client or server error responses."}, {"id": "30", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/help.html", "param": "x-content-type-options", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/help.html", "otherinfo": "This issue still applies to error type pages (401, 403, 500, etc.) as those pages are often still affected by injection issues, in which case there is still concern for browsers sniffing pages away from their actual content type.\\nAt \\"High\\" threshold this scan rule will not alert on client or server error responses."}, {"id": "36", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/index.html", "param": "x-content-type-options", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/index.html", "otherinfo": "This issue still applies to error type pages (401, 403, 500, etc.) as those pages are often still affected by injection issues, in which case there is still concern for browsers sniffing pages away from their actual content type.\\nAt \\"High\\" threshold this scan rule will not alert on client or server error responses."}, {"id": "22", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/resources/css/main.css", "param": "x-content-type-options", "attack": "", "method": "GET", "evidence": "", "nodeName": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/resources/css/main.css", "otherinfo": "This issue still applies to error type pages (401, 403, 500, etc.) as those pages are often still affected by injection issues, in which case there is still concern for browsers sniffing pages away from their actual content type.\\nAt \\"High\\" threshold this scan rule will not alert on client or server error responses."}, {"id": "28", "uri": "http://zero.webappsecurity.com/resources/img/main_carou