fd2b0c2c-7e39-4ee0-acb8-7ca406258b2d	00e56846-b7b1-43ce-96a7-7ddce76d2461	9bf4912c-31a7-4640-8c18-5f0e8fda9952	Remote Code Execution via Log4Shell Vulnerability	The vulnerable application utilizes a logging module that incorporates Log4j, which has been identified as vulnerable to the Log4Shell vulnerability (CVE-2021-44228). An attacker can execute arbitrary code on the target system by injecting malicious input into the logging mechanism, resulting in a remote code execution vulnerability.	critical	verified	9.8	CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H	CVE-2021-44228	f	CWE-502	A09:2021	logging module		1. Identify a logging endpoint or a component that utilizes the logging module. 2. Craft a malicious payload that injects a JNDI lookup, pointing to a malicious LDAP server. 3. Send the crafted payload to the identified endpoint. 4. The vulnerable Log4j library will perform the JNDI lookup, leading to the execution of the attacker's code.	This vulnerability allows an attacker to execute arbitrary code on the target system, resulting in full system compromise. This has severe security and business implications as an attacker can steal sensitive data, disrupt system operations, or use the compromised system as a pivot point for further attacks.	1. Update the Log4j library to a version that has fixed the Log4Shell vulnerability (version 2.15.0 or later). 2. If updating is not feasible, set the system property `log4j2.formatMsgNoLookups` to `true` to mitigate the vulnerability.	{https://nvd.nist.gov/v1/nvdapi/v1/cve/2021-44228,https://log4j.apache.org/security.html,https://owasp.org/Top10/A09_2021-Security_Logs_and_Monitoring_Failures/}	\N	72f5b2aa-8dc5-47f0-8f38-8c4456c3d10c	f9808aaa-d2c5-4525-828d-616b9b8c594f	\N	t	llama-3.3-70b-versatile	\N	\N	\N	3	2026-05-14 05:25:18.963869+00	2026-05-27 06:18:09.388701+00	VAPT-1019	\N	start working on this findings 	\N	\N	\N
